%% section: Termination, and the rolling-update 502
%% caption: Where the rolling-update 502 comes from
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant K as kubelet
    participant EP as Endpoints
    participant PX as kube-proxy
    participant P as Pod
    participant C as Client
    K->>P: SIGTERM
    K->>EP: mark the pod terminating
    par these race
        EP->>PX: update rules on every node
        P->>P: begins shutting down
    end
    C->>PX: request
    PX->>P: routed to a pod that is already closing
    P-->>C: 502
    Note over EP,PX: endpoint propagation is not instant — the pod must keep serving through it
    Note over P: fix: preStop sleep, so the pod stays up while the rules catch up
